# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# IMPORTANT: this uses `text=auto`, NOT `text`. The previous rule was
# `* text eol=lf`, which FORCES text treatment on every file in the repo and
# only exempted *.png. Git then applied CRLF -> LF normalisation to binary
# assets on check-in, silently deleting every CR byte that happened to sit
# before an LF. That destroyed public/CLO3D.mp4 twice: the stored blob had
# ~56 bytes removed from the middle of the H.264 stream, which shifted every
# subsequent NAL length prefix and left roughly one second of playable video.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect binary content and leave it alone, and the
# explicit `binary` rules below make that guarantee unconditional for the
# asset types this project ships.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary

# Video / audio
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mov binary
*.m4v binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary

# Fonts
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Archives / documents
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
